openwrt_wiki_nanostationm5.Nanostation Loco M5 Serial Pins:
A pin header can be soldered to the board to use the serial port. The board is mounted to a sled which can be pulled out after the protective cover for the RJ-45 port and the screw (under the label) is removed.

If your adapter requires the board's 3.3V, the board may not boot (stalls after U-Boot's "DRAM:   4 MB" message). If this happens, re-apply power after removing the adapter and only plug it in after the second LED has turned on.

{{:media:ubiquiti:nanostation_loco_m5_serial.jpg?400|}}

openwrt_wiki_nanostationm2.Flashing via AirOS web gui:
This method is only available for devices with airOS versions before 6.1.7.

  - Downgrade airOS via tftp or web as requested in the preparations\\ {{media:ubiquiti:nanom2-downgrade.png?600|Flashing via AirOS web gui}}
  - Go to Firmware Update, select the firmware image file with Upload Firmware (''openwrt-version-ath79-generic-ubnt-nano-m-squashfs-factory.bin''), and click update:\\ {{media:ubiquiti:nanostation_loco_m2.png?600|Flashing via AirOS web gui}}\\

